{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>יצא</b> — Rabbi Moses said: עינימו [their eye] is like the appearance of crystal; from the abundance of fat it came forth and the eye appeared beautiful to behold. And some say: from the abundance of their fat, it is as though their eye came forth, in the manner of: עינים להם ולא יראו [they have eyes but do not see]." "<b>And the word משכיות</b> — according to Rabbi Moses' opinion: like thoughts, for שכוי is a designation for the heart, combining two meanings into one, as in the Targum of יצף [he shields]; as though משכיות [were] מראות [visions], like: ולבי ראה הרבה חכמה ודעת [and my heart saw much wisdom and knowledge]. And the meaning of שכית חמדה [coveted object] may apply, or it may be in the sense of ואבן משכית מצוירת [a painted touchstone], and the paintings are the thoughts." "<b>And the meaning of עברו</b> — that they pass beyond what human beings can comprehend."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 73, :notes {1 "The verse under discussion reads משכיות לבבם; Ibn Ezra parses whether משכיות modifies לבבם or stands independently. The argument pivots on whether שכוי/שכית denotes the heart, an object of desire, or a painted stone."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:11.907269805Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}